        {
          "row": 2,
          "col": 0,
          "html": "<strong>psuX-max-power</strong><br/><strong>jack-max-power</strong><br/><strong>2pin-max-power</strong>"
        },
        {
          "row": 6,
          "col": 0,
          "html": "<strong>psuX-poe-out-max-power</strong><br/><strong>jack-poe-out-max-power</strong><br/><strong>2pin-poe-out-max-power</strong><br/><strong>poe-in-poe-out-max-power</strong>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "rows": 6,
      "cols": 2,
      "official_wide": false,
      "md_wide": false,
      "cells": [
        {
          "row": 3,
          "col": 1,
          "html": "Specifies PoE out state<ul><li>auto-on - the resistance on the port is checked first, and power is applied only if it is in the range from 3kΩ to 26.5kΩ</li><li>forced-on - resistance detection is disabled and power is always provided on pair B (alt)</li><li>off - all detection and power is turned off for this port</li></ul>Additional states on PSEs that support 802.3bt PoE out:<ul><li>forced-on-a - same as forced-on, but power is provided on pair A (main)</li><li>forced-on-bt - same as forced-on, but power is provided on all 4 pairs (available only from the CLI, this state cannot be selected in Winbox/WebFig)</li></ul><strong>Note:</strong> Short-circuit and overload protection is always on, independently of the selected PoE out state."
        },
        {
          "row": 4,
          "col": 1,
          "html": "poe-priority specifies the importance of PoE out ports, in cases when a total PoE out limit is reached, the interface with the lowest port priority will be powered off first. Highest priority is 0, the lowest priority is 99. If there are 2 or more ports with the same priority then the port with the smallest port number will have a higher priority. <br/>Every 6 seconds ports will be checked for a possibility to provide PoE out if it was turned off due to port priority."
        }
      ]
    },
